---
import PageFrame from "../components/PageFrame.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Logos AI Pricing"
  description="Choose between the free reader, your own API key, or a managed Logos AI experience."
>
  <PageFrame current="pricing">
    <main class="shell py-16">
      <section class="max-w-4xl animate-rise">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 section-title">Choose the setup that fits how you study.</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 section-copy">
          Start free in the web reader or desktop app, bring your own key if you want full control, or use managed
          access when you want everything configured for you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-muted">Free</p>
          <div class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl text-text">$0</div>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Read Scripture in the browser, download the desktop app, and start studying without paying first.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
            <li>Full web reader</li>
            <li>Downloadable desktop app</li>
            <li>Basic study tools</li>
            <li>Simple, low-friction onboarding</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="surface-card border-accent/40 bg-accent/5 p-8">
          <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-accent">Bring Your Own Key</p>
          <div class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl text-text">Control</div>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Connect your own provider and unlock advanced AI features on your own terms.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
            <li>Best fit for technical users</li>
            <li>Bring your own limits and provider settings</li>
            <li>Works well with local or self-managed workflows</li>
            <li>Guided setup in the docs</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="surface-card border-gold/40 bg-gold/5 p-8">
          <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-gold">Managed</p>
          <div class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl text-text">Simple plans</div>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Let Logos AI handle the setup so you can open the app and start studying immediately.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
            <li>Hosted AI access</li>
            <li>No API key setup</li>
            <li>Saved history and richer study tools</li>
            <li>Priority usage and premium convenience features</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow">Optional Upgrades</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-text">Add depth when you need it.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            As Logos AI grows, optional packs can focus on deeper study, sermon prep, original languages, church tools,
            exports, and premium voices without making the free experience feel stripped down.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow">Best With Desktop</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-text">The deeper workflow lives in the app.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            The web reader is the fastest way to start. The downloadable app is where Logos Chat, local AI, read-aloud,
            offline-friendly study, and longer-form workflows make the most sense.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </PageFrame>
</SiteLayout>
